# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 006
# Act: INS−  (Instance aimed at Ground)   Stance: Cultivating   Site: Void
#
# The Existence triad's third and final operator, first use. SIG "produces
# the sign"; INS "produces the anchor" — a content-addressed hash, frame-
# independent and immutable, unlike SIG's mutable, frame-dependent name
# (EO Event Streaming §3.1). INS− is the move before any anchor is
# actually minted: cultivating the ground on which an anchor-worthy entity
# could stand at all.
#
# Earning argument: precondition is turn-5 (SIG*) having earned a STABLE
# sign across a kind — an anchor minted against a sign that still might
# flicker between instances would be anchoring something that isn't yet
# one thing. Turn-5 is exactly what makes "one thing" a true claim here:
# the same sign, "absent", holds across every member of the kind.
#
# What this does NOT claim: no anchor exists yet. Cultivating the ground
# is not minting the entity — that is INS+, next.

:turn-6  eot:opens        :turn-5 .
:turn-6  eot:act          eot:INS- .
:turn-6  eot:stance       "Cultivating" .
:turn-6  eot:site         "Void" .
:turn-6  eot:cultivates   "the stable sign traced in turn-5, as an anchor candidate" .
:turn-6  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
